W: 2. I'll sell my rod, I'll sell my reel
W: I'll sell my only spinning wheel
W: To by my love a sword of steel
W: Iss guh day thoo a voorneen slawn.
W:
W: Chorus:
W: Shule, shule, shule aroon
W: Shule go succir agus, shule go kewn;
W: Shule go dheen durrus oggus aylig lume,
W: Iss guh day thoo avorneen slawn.
W:
W: 3. I'll dye my petticoats, I'll dye them red
W: And through the streets I'll beg my bread,
W: Until my parents shall wish me dead
W: Iss guh day thoo a voorneen slawn.
W: (Chorus)
W:
W: 4. I wish, I wish, I wish in vain
W: I wish I had my heart again,
W: And vainly think I'd not complain
W: Iss guh day thoo a voorneen slawn.
W: (Chorus)
W:
W: 5. But now my love has gone to France
W: To try his fortune to advance.
W: If he e'er come back, 'tis but a chance
W: Iss guh day thoo a voorneen slawn.
W: (Chorus)
W:
W: 6. Come, come, come O love,
W: Quickly come to me, softly move,
W: Come to the door and away we'll flee,
W: And safe forever may my darling be.
W: (Chorus)
